E={'2528': 'CDIAL 2528 ēvam ēva discusses kab/kabe and jab only as formations crossed with interrogative ka or relative ya. The unsplit now/just-so parent alone omits this essential pronominal component; a compound or precise construction analysis is needed.', '9198': 'CDIAL 9198.1 *bā “father” explicitly gives Nepali bā and bājyā “grandfather”. Its mother branch is separately numbered 9198.2 *bāī; sister or honorific woman senses require distinguishing other bāī families.', '3164': 'CDIAL 3164 kim explicitly gives northern and eastern ki/kī “what”, Hindi and Kumauni kyā, and Middle Indo-Aryan ki/kiṃ. The interrogative sense excludes the borrowed Persian conjunction ki.', '9875': 'CDIAL 9875.1 marīca gives miri “pepper”, while section 2 *maricca gives Assamese maris, Bihari mirca/miric and Maithili mircāi. The selected chili terms must preserve this distinction; modern pepper-to-chili semantic transfer is explicitly represented by the cited comparanda.', '6770': 'CDIAL 6770.1 *dhāgga gives Hindi dhāgā, Nepali dhāgo and Punjabi dhāggā “thread”. The addendum revises the deeper reconstruction toward *dhārga/*dharga; this family link retains that uncertainty and any intra-IA diffusion.', '5090': 'CDIAL 5090 separates short-vowel jaḍa, geminate *jaḍḍa and u-vowel *jūḍa. Its section 4 explicitly gives Maithili jūṛ/jūr and Hindi jūṛ “cold”; a-vowel jar without decisive quantity/local evidence remains ambiguous between the first two branches.', '6010': 'CDIAL 6010 gives Punjabi tāgā/taggā, Hindi/Bengali tāgā and Nepali tāgā “thread”, from a reconstructed *trāgga/*tārga/*tāgra family. The alternatives concern the reconstructed cluster; all selected survey forms continue the same documented thread family.', '8265': 'CDIAL 8265 putra explicitly gives put/puttar/pūt and northern pūc̣/pūṣ, alongside Palula putr and the wider son family. Punjabi-mediated puttar is explicitly allowed by the addendum; a bare pū requires separate local contraction evidence.', '12278': 'CDIAL 12278 śata explicitly gives Bengali sa, Marathi śẽ, Maiya/Shina šal and western sau “hundred”. These numeral forms identify the family; no composite hundred-and numeral is included.', '9188': 'CDIAL 9188 bahukāra gives buhārī/bahārī/bohārī “broom”, but very contracted bari may also converge with the vardhanī broom family. Retained buh/bahār material supports the first family; the contracted forms remain a competing-root question.', '10066': 'CDIAL 10066 mārayati explicitly gives the widespread mār- kill/strike verb, including western mārṇā and Hindi mārnā. Survey mar/mara/mariyo forms are ordinary inflections; the kill gloss distinguishes the transitive verb from the related die paradigm.', '13574': 'CDIAL 13574 separately numbers sūra, sūrya and sūriya. The survey suraj/suruj forms contain additional j material absent from the bare sūra parent, and suriya selects its separately numbered branch; these cannot be copied to the broad head.', '5071': 'CDIAL 5071 *chōṭṭa explicitly gives Hindi choṭā, Nepali choṭo and Kashmiri choṭ “short, small”. The selected small/short responses fit this lexical family, while the addendum distinguishes unaspirated *cōṭa and other child-name formations.', '4137': 'CDIAL 4137 *gāra explicitly gives Hindi gārā, Nepali gāro and regional gārā “mud, mortar”, retaining a conjectural deeper formation. The survey mud sense fits the documented material noun.', '11366': 'CDIAL 11366 vartman gives bāṭ/vāṭ “path” but expressly states that some feminine forms may equally derive from vartis. That alternative must be checked locally before assigning the existing broad path link.', '9828': 'CDIAL 9828 manuṣya documents manus and Palula meš, while explicitly qualifying several māś/moš forms through mānuṣa or martya. The clear manus/paradigmatic forms can be linked; unresolved short forms retain the competing-root qualification.', '1135': 'CDIAL 1135.1 ātman explicitly gives Hindi āp respectful “you”, Punjabi āpā̃ “we” and Old Marwari āpa “self, you, we”. These survey pronouns belong to the reflexive-to-personal paradigm; the distinct possessive *ātmanaka subsection is not selected.', '5239': 'CDIAL 5239 jīva explicitly includes Nepali jiu “body, life”, Oriya jī “heart” and the addendum’s Western Pahari jiu “mind, heart, person”. The survey jiv/jiu body/heart polysemy therefore has primary comparative support.', '9479': 'CDIAL 9479 bhāṣā gives Middle Indo-Aryan bhāsā “speech, language” and modern bhās/bhāś. Full bhāsā may be learned or renewed across Indo-Aryan; the family link leaves that route open.', '4313': 'CDIAL 4313 gōrūpa gives Prakrit gōru and widespread goru/guru “cow, ox, cattle”, including explicit cow uses in Kumauni, Kashmiri and Hindi. It preserves the full cattle compound rather than linking its modern continuations to bare go.', '4435': 'CDIAL 4435 *gharapāla “house guardian” explicitly gives Hindi gharwālā “husband” and gharwālī “wife”, alongside Sindhi gharavāro. The full survey gharval- household terms fit that compound family; the modern suffix may have been renewed or transmitted regionally.', '8179': 'CDIAL 8179 pitṛ explicitly gives nominative pitā and Middle Indo-Aryan piu, followed by Punjabi peo/piu and Lahnda pio “father”. The survey pe/pio and learned pitā forms identify this kinship family without equating them with unrelated nursery terms.', '6141': 'CDIAL 6141 dadāti explicitly describes the give paradigm’s dēti and dēhi remodeling and regional deh/de/do forms. Past-only di may instead require the separately treated participial family, so that ambiguity is retained.', '4918': 'CDIAL 4918 cōkṣa gives Sindhi cokho and Gujarati cokhā “cleaned rice”, alongside the pure/clean/good adjective. The survey rice forms support this semantic specialization; the underlying food sense is explicitly attested, not inferred solely from clean.', '11580': 'CDIAL 11580 vālukā gives Hindi bārū, regional bālu and an explicit suffix replacement vālikā accounting for Bengali/Oriya bāli “sand”. No separate stored vālikā subsection exists; the evidence specifies that replacement for i-ending forms.', '6495': 'CDIAL 6495 dūra gives dūr/dūri/dūro “far” and explicitly records retroflex ḍūr in the addendum. The simple survey forms fit; dūrāī contains additional nominalizing material whose analysis remains separate.', '9349': 'CDIAL 9349 bhaginī explicitly gives the bahin/bhaṇ/bheṇ “sister” family and discusses honorific address to women, but bare bai can converge with the nursery bāī family. The n-bearing sister forms are distinguishable; bare bai woman forms require local historical evidence.', '5301': 'CDIAL 5301.1 jyotsnā explicitly gives Nepali jun, Assamese zon and Halbi jon “moon”, contrasting the separately numbered initial-y *yotsnā branch. The j/z-bearing survey forms select the base branch.', '5550': 'CDIAL 5550 ḍimba explicitly gives Bengali ḍim, Assamese ḍimā and Oriya ḍimba “egg”. Dental transcription in dima is retained as a local phonetic qualification; the egg-word family is identifiable.', '9883': 'CDIAL 9883 markaṭa² explicitly gives Hindi makṛī, Punjabi makkaṛī, Nepali mākuro and Oriya makaṛā “spider”. The survey k-r/ḍ spider variants fit the documented family; its relation to other insect-name reconstructions remains qualified.'}
qs=[];ix={};acc=[];held=[];current={r['Form_ID'] for r in csv.DictReader((ROOT/'data/etymology-assignments.csv').open()) if r['Status']=='accepted' and r['Rank']=='1'}
for x in json.loads((P/'global-exact-candidates.json').read_text()):
 if len(x['parents'])!=1 or x['parents'][0] not in E:continue
 k=x['parents'][0];r=x['record'];w=norm(r['Form']);target=k;reason=None
 if r['ID'] in current:continue
 if k in {'2528','13574','11366'}:reason=E[k]
 elif k=='9198' and r['Gloss'] not in {'father','grandfather'}:reason='Sister/mother/woman meanings need the distinct bāī or bhaginī family, not *bā father.'
 elif k=='9875':
  if w=='miri':target=k
  elif w in {'maras','mirchai','mircha'}:target='9875-2'
  else:reason='Pepper branch remains unresolved.'
 elif k=='5090':
  if w=='jur':target='5090-4'
  else:reason='The a-vowel cold forms can continue jaḍa or *jaḍḍa; vowel quantity and local development must choose the branch.'
 elif k=='8265' and w=='pu':reason='The bare pu son form needs a local account of final-consonant loss.'
 elif k=='9188':reason='Contracted bari/bahri broom forms can converge with vardhanī; choose the lexical family with local evidence.'
 elif k=='5071' and not w.startswith('ch'):reason='Unaspirated small forms may select a separately reconstructed cōṭa family in the addendum.'
 elif k=='9828' and (w not in {'manus','meś'}):reason='Short man/person form retains competing mānuṣa/martya or unexplained extension; the broad older manuṣya link is not decisive.'
 elif k=='4435' and w=='garala':reason='Contracted garala husband needs confirmation of the complete household compound.'
 elif k=='6141' and ('gave' in r['Gloss'] or w=='di'):reason='Past give forms require comparison with the separate datta/*dita paradigm; do not attach by present-stem resemblance alone.'
 elif k=='6495' and w=='durai':reason='The extended durai distance noun requires local suffix/derivational analysis.'
 elif k=='9349' and not any(c in w for c in 'nṇ'):reason='Bare bai woman forms compete with the nursery bāī family.'
 if re.search('uncertain|unresolved|illegible|unreadable',r['Tags']+' '+r['Description'],re.I) and r['Language_ID']!='Rana':reason=reason or 'Source uncertainty requires local review.'
 if (k,target) not in ix:ix[k,target]=len(qs);qs.append(dict(parent=target,citation='CDIAL['+target.replace('-','.',1)+']',evidence=E[k]))
 i=ix[k,target]
 if reason:held.append(dict(record=r,families=[i],reason=reason,passNumber=23));continue
 ev=E[k]+' Uncertain transfer between Indo-Aryan languages does not prevent this supported family link under the user’s preference.'
 if r['Language_ID']=='Rana' and 'uncertain' in r['Tags']:ev+=' RNS uncertainty concerns locality attribution, not the lexical reading, according to the source audit.'
 acc.append(dict(record=r,family=i,parent=target,citation=qs[i]['citation'],evidence=ev))
(P/'global-fifth-rules.json').write_text(json.dumps(qs,ensure_ascii=False,indent=1));(P/'global-fifth-decisions.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(accepted=acc,held=held),ensure_ascii=False,indent=1));(P/'global_fifth_save.py').write_text((P/'sixth_save.py').read_text().replace('sixth-save-decisions.json','global-fifth-decisions.json').replace('sixth','global-fifth'))
print('accepted',len(acc),'held',len(held))
from collections import Counter
print(Counter(x['parent'] for x in acc))
